<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">31 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 31 May, from 1223 to 1970.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/cumans" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cumans.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1223">1223 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">803 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols rout the Rus and Cumans at the Kalka River</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Mongol expedition under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebe">Jebe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a> crushed the armies of several Rus princes and their Cuman allies. The full Mongol conquest of the Rus lands came fourteen years later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1578">1578 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">448 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Martin Frobisher sails on his third Arctic voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frobisher left Harwich with fifteen ships to mine what he believed was gold ore on Baffin Island. The ore proved worthless, and the Northwest Passage stayed unfound.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1790">1790 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">236 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington signs the first US copyright law</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Copyright Act protected books, maps and charts for 14 years, renewable once. It drew on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s Statute of Anne and founded American copyright law.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1859">1859 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">167 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Clock of Westminster starts keeping time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The clock in the new tower of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palace-of-westminster">Houses of Parliament</a> began running. Its great bell, Big Ben, struck the hours for the first time that July.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1902">1902 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">124 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Vereeniging ends the South African War</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> leaders accepted British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a> and Orange Free State in return for promises of self-government. The war had cost tens of thousands of lives, many in British camps.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British and German fleets clash at Jutland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The largest naval battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> lose more ships and men, but the German High Seas Fleet withdrew to port and rarely ventured out again.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1970">1970 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake and avalanche devastate northern Peru</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.9 earthquake set off an avalanche from Huascarán that buried the town of Yungay. About 70,000 people died, making it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>'s worst natural disaster.</p></div></li></ol>
